      <section class="tale-chapter" id="introduction"><div class="tale-chapter-heading"><span>01</span><h2>A small beginning,<br><em>a continuing seva.</em></h2></div><p>Jay Bhole Group began in 2006 with a small collection of Shiv bhakts of Shri Neelkanth Mahadev. Its work brings devotional practice into tangible form: sacred designs, ritual objects, community activity and shared journeys of worship.</p><p>This page is a contributed visual archive. The descriptions identify the work shown in the supplied photographs and keep the group’s own official website as the source for its introduction, history and contact details.</p><a class="cosmology-source" href="https://www.jaybholegroup.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the group’s full official introduction →</a></section>
      <section class="tale-chapter jay-bhole-works" id="works"><div class="tale-chapter-heading"><span>02</span><h2>Works of devotion<br><em>and craft.</em></h2></div><p>Each piece below is presented as a work of Jay Bhole Group Ahmedabad, using the names and descriptions confirmed by the group.</p>
        <div class="work-entry"><figure><img src="/assets/images/jay-bhole-sand-sri-yantra.jpg" alt="Sand Sri Yantra created by Jay Bhole Group Ahmedabad" width="2295" height="4080" loading="lazy"><figcaption>SAND SRI YANTRA · CONTRIBUTED PHOTOGRAPH</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">SRI YANTRA</p><h3>Sand Sri Yantra</h3><p>A sacred geometric work made in sand, recorded as part of the group’s Sri Yantra work.</p></div></div>
        <div class="work-entry"><figure><img src="/assets/images/jay-bhole-chamar.jpg" alt="Chamar made by Jay Bhole Group Ahmedabad" width="896" height="512" loading="lazy"><figcaption>CHAMAR · CONTRIBUTED PHOTOGRAPH</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">CEREMONIAL WORK</p><h3>Chamar</h3><p>A ceremonial chamar made as part of the group’s devotional craftsmanship.</p></div></div>
        <div class="work-entry"><figure><img src="/assets/images/jay-bhole-ghanta.png" alt="Panch Dhatu Ghanta made by Jay Bhole Group Ahmedabad" width="419" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>GHANTA · PANCH DHATU · CONTRIBUTED IMAGE</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">PANCH DHATU</p><h3>Ghanta</h3><p>A bell work made in Panch Dhatu, the five-metal tradition named by the group.</p></div></div>
        <div class="work-entry"><figure><img src="/assets/images/jay-bhole-paduka-detail.jpg" alt="Decorated Paduka made by Jay Bhole Group Ahmedabad" width="1908" height="1312" loading="lazy"><img src="/assets/images/jay-bhole-paduka-ceremony.jpg" alt="Jay Bhole Group Paduka presented with flowers and ceremonial cloth" width="1920" height="1280" loading="lazy"><figcaption>PADUKA · CONTRIBUTED PHOTOGRAPHS</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">SACRED FOOTPRINTS</p><h3>Paduka</h3><p>Decorated Paduka photographed close-up and during a ceremonial presentation with flowers and sacred cloth.</p></div></div>
        <div class="work-entry"><figure><img src="/assets/images/jay-bhole-ajay-baan.jpg" alt="Ajay Baan display created by Jay Bhole Group Ahmedabad" width="847" height="1280" loading="lazy"><figcaption>AJAY BAAN · CONTRIBUTED PHOTOGRAPH</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">AMBaji TRADITION</p><h3>Ajay Baan</h3><p>A devotional display and information panel for the Ajay Baan associated with Ambaji.</p></div></div>
        <div class="work-entry"><figure><img src="/assets/images/jay-bhole-akhand-bharat.jpg" alt="Akhand Bharat handcrafted work by Jay Bhole Group Ahmedabad" width="2232" height="2922" loading="lazy"><figcaption>AKHAND BHARAT · CONTRIBUTED PHOTOGRAPH</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">HANDCRAFTED MAP</p><h3>Akhand Bharat</h3><p>A handcrafted Akhand Bharat work documented as part of the group’s devotional and cultural creations.</p></div></div>
      </section>
      <section class="tale-chapter" id="witness"><div class="tale-chapter-heading"><span>03</span><h2>A design<br><em>received with approval.</em></h2></div><figure class="tale-inline"><img src="/assets/images/jay-bhole-jagadguru.jpg" alt="Jay Bhole Group members with Jagadguru Shankaracharya Sri Vidhushekhara Bharati Mahaswamiji" width="2418" height="1788" loading="lazy"><figcaption>JAGADGURU SHANKARACHARYA SRI VIDHUSHEKHARA BHARATI MAHASWAMIJI WITH GROUP MEMBERS · CONTRIBUTED PHOTOGRAPH</figcaption></figure><p>The group identifies this photograph as a moment with Jagadguru Shankaracharya Sri Vidhushekhara Bharati Mahaswamiji, who approved the design of the Sri Yantras made by the group.</p></section>
